      "payload": "{\"kind\":\"review_result\",\"review_result\":\"{\\\"evidence_run\\\": \\\"b1fc3cba2a86ab3e6d21317861d7e1cea3d334690e5640b94e1dd82747c33e20\\\", \\\"findings\\\": [{\\\"control\\\": \\\"CC6.1\\\", \\\"evidence_node\\\": \\\"8ae6499bd7a857b45e2c911eda407e539b5a0e5c4d793fc4d5b734053e24108d\\\", \\\"policy_clause\\\": \\\"AICPA Trust Services Criteria CC6.1 (Logical Access Controls)\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"According to the SOC 2 report (acme-soc2-2026, issued 2026-06-30) and penetration test (acme-pen-test-2026-07, issued 2026-07-15), multi-factor authentication is not enforced on the legacy customer tier, allowing single-factor authentication for certain accounts.\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, {\\\"control\\\": \\\"CC6.1\\\", \\\"evidence_node\\\": \\\"65a5fc8e7c43d1faa47d5be0d74091a3274847ad2b0b4b572262ef01b408b705\\\", \\\"policy_clause\\\": \\\"AICPA Trust Services Criteria CC6.1 (Logical Access Controls)\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The penetration test report (acme-pen-test-2026-07, issued 2026-07-15) identified that a session cookie is missing the SameSite attribute on one legacy endpoint, which is a carried-over finding that has not been remediated.\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, {\\\"control\\\": \\\"EVIDENCE-STALE\\\", \\\"evidence_node\\\": \\\"65a5fc8e7c43d1faa47d5be0d74091a3274847ad2b0b4b572262ef01b408b705\\\", \\\"policy_clause\\\": \\\"Temporal validity threshold (minimum 0.5)\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The penetration test report (acme-pen-test-2025-02, issued 2025-02-10) was pruned as stale due to low temporal validity (0.342). Recommend re-acquisition of an updated penetration test.\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, {\\\"control\\\": \\\"DPA \\\\u00a77.1\\\", \\\"evidence_node\\\": \\\"8ae6499bd7a857b45e2c911eda407e539b5a0e5c4d793fc4d5b734053e24108d\\\", \\\"policy_clause\\\": \\\"Clause 7.1 (Technical and Organizational Security Measures)\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The DPA commits to implementing appropriate technical and organizational measures and access controls (Clause 7.1), but the SOC 2 report (acme-soc2-2026) reveals a logical access control exception where MFA is not enforced on the legacy customer tier.\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, {\\\"control\\\": \\\"DPA \\\\u00a75.1\\\", \\\"evidence_node\\\": \\\"6b2e0019cf0e1c9e3ec2b377d30cda4f6314be5a00eb10ff0ab9296b525959a7\\\", \\\"policy_clause\\\": \\\"Clause 5.1 (Subprocessor List Maintenance)\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"While Clause 5.1 of the DPA states that the Processor maintains a current list of subprocessors, the list itself was not provided in the reviewed materials to verify compliance with the US/EU data residency restrictions in Clause 4.1.\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\"}], \\\"risk_score\\\": 0.65, \\\"vendor_id\\\": \\\"acme-saas-inc\\\"}\",\"vendor_id\":\"acme-saas-inc\"}",
      "result": null,
